% expect-output: 0.7313537
% expect-output: -0.6819984
% expect-output: 0.17364818
% Scenario: a large angle. `sin` and `cos` reduce their argument modulo
% 360 degrees in double precision before the conversion to radians, so
% -168437 degrees is 43, 168437 is 317, and a million is 280, each with
% single precision's digits; converting first would lose the third
% digit at a million degrees.
389 -433 mul cos =
168437 sin =
1000000 cos =
